# Anti-Hang Stable Hook Interface

Semantic owner: CURRENT `ANTI_HANG_RUNTIME`.
Executable source: `true-memory/runtime/anti_hang_kernel.py` and mirrored plugin `scripts/runtime_kernel.py`.

Preferred call:
`hook(event, state)`.

Events:
`TASK_ENTRY | BEFORE_ACTION | AFTER_ACTION | AFTER_MATERIAL_RETURN | PRESSURE | BEFORE_USER_RETURN | USER_STOP`.

Legacy pure helpers remain implementation primitives only:
`replay_gate | effect_transition | runnable_scan | reconcile_eligibility | return_gate | pressure_policy`.

Correctness is behavioral:
- never blind-replay ambiguous consequential effects;
- never hide risky preparation + consequential write + readback in one opaque composite;
- nonterminal effect blocks only dependent frontier;
- no immediate unchanged polling without material wake;
- every material/action return re-enters root;
- pressure rotates/narrows safe cycles and auto-continues;
- user-visible global return is allowed only at completion, explicit Stop, true gate, or proven external quiescence;
- explicit Stop prevents new operations and does not imply remote cancellation.

Task decomposition, cognitive hooks, memory lifecycle, route strategy and message rendering are outside Anti-Hang ownership.

